#   node prisma/demo.mjs            create them
#   node prisma/demo.mjs --remove   delete them and free their seats
#
# Unlike everything above, these are not environment variables — they are
# comments, so copying this file to .env.local cannot load them. They are
# written here because this is the file that says what you need to run the
# project, but note what that means: .env.example is the one env file meant to
# be committed, so a National Coordinator password now lives in the repo. It is
# only ever as harmless as the database it points at.
